{"availability":"available","full":"gatling/gatling","name":"gatling","description":"Modern Load Testing as Code","category":"Developer tools","language":"Scala","stars":6958,"forks":1207,"created":"2011-05-31T12:40:25Z","updated":"2026-10-05T08:58:38Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://gatling.io","topics":["automation","cicd","gatling","java","javascript","kotlin","load-test","load-testing","load-tests","loadtest","loadtesting","loadtests","netty","performance-test","performance-test-gatling","performance-testing","performance-tests","scala","typescript"],"demo":"https://gatling.io/gatling-enterprise-load-testing-live-demo?utm_campaign=oss&utm_source=github&utm_medium=gatling&utm_content=nav","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:29.705Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:29.705Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:29.705Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:23:29.705Z","stars":6958,"forks":1207}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Gatling is an open-source load testing tool. You write test scenarios (\"simulations\") as code, run them against your services, and get a detailed HTML report of response times, throughput, and errors. This repository is Gatling Community Edition, licensed under Apache 2.0 and free to use, including commercially.","An engine that does not need a fleet. Virtual users are lightweight messages on a non-blocking engine built on Netty, not operating system threads. Tools built on a thread-per-user model need a fleet of load generators to reach the same load.","Tests are code, in your repository. Readable diffs, reviewable pull requests, and the same review process as the application they test. No proprietary XML format, no export step between a GUI and your pipeline."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gatling/gatling/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2b21c6295fae09e7143c604e502846c1d27ccf9e7477086e03e43473f3a3b2cb","extractedAt":"2026-1